MONGODB AND CASSANDRA LAB PRACTICALS
====================================

PART A: DOCKER SETUP
====================

1. Check Docker version
docker --version

2. Download MongoDB image
docker pull mongo

3. Run MongoDB container
docker run -d --name mongodb -p 27017:27017 mongo

4. Check running containers
docker ps

5. Open MongoDB shell
docker exec -it mongodb mongosh

6. Stop and start MongoDB container
docker stop mongodb
docker start mongodb

7. View MongoDB logs
docker logs mongodb

8. Download and run Cassandra
docker pull cassandra:5.0
docker run -d --name cassandra-db -p 9042:9042 cassandra:5.0

9. Open Cassandra shell
docker exec -it cassandra-db cqlsh

10. Stop and start Cassandra container
docker stop cassandra-db
docker start cassandra-db

Note: Cassandra may take several minutes to start for the first time. Check with:
docker logs -f cassandra-db
Press Ctrl+C to stop viewing logs; the container continues running.


