PART F: MONGODB UPDATE OPERATORS
================================

Q1. $set — Set marks of roll number 101 to 90.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$set: {marks: 90}})

Q2. $unset — Remove city from roll number 101.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$unset: {city: ""}})

Q3. $inc — Increase fees of roll number 101 by 5000.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$inc: {fees: 5000}})

Q4. $mul — Double fees of roll number 101.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$mul: {fees: 2}})

Q5. $rename — Rename marks to score for roll number 101.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$rename: {marks: "score"}})

Q6. $min — Set CGPA to 7.5 only if it is lower than the existing value.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$min: {cgpa: 7.5}})

Q7. $max — Set marks to 95 only if 95 is greater than the existing value.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$max: {marks: 95}})

Q8. $currentDate — Set lastModified to the current date and time.
db.students.updateOne({rollNo: 101}, {$currentDate: {lastModified: true}})

Note: These updates are separate practical questions. Run each independently if you need the original field values. If you run Q5, the marks field becomes score.


