PART N: IMPORTANT VIVA POINTS
=============================

1. MongoDB stores flexible BSON documents; Cassandra is a distributed wide-column NoSQL database.
2. MongoDB shell: mongosh. Cassandra shell: cqlsh.
3. MongoDB query methods: find(), insertMany(), updateOne(), deleteOne(), aggregate().
4. Cassandra commands: SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE.
5. MongoDB comparison operators: $gt, $lt, $gte, $lte, $ne.
6. MongoDB logical operators: $and, $or, $not, $nor.
7. MongoDB projection includes fields with 1 and excludes fields with 0. Do not mix inclusion and exclusion in one projection, except for _id.
8. MongoDB aggregation: $match filters, $group groups, $sum counts/sums, $push builds arrays, $$ROOT represents the whole document.
9. MongoDB $unwind separates array elements into individual pipeline documents.
10. Cassandra primary keys identify rows. ALLOW FILTERING may be inefficient and should be used cautiously.
11. Docker commands:
    docker ps
    docker ps -a
    docker start mongodb
    docker stop mongodb
    docker exec -it mongodb mongosh
    docker start cassandra-db
    docker stop cassandra-db
    docker exec -it cassandra-db cqlsh
